From: Second Chapter
Subject: [PATCH] soc/tegra: pmc: power off grouper instead of restarting

Google's bootloader has a battery-status mode the kernel reboots into on
power-off when USB is connected. U-Boot lacks it and boots normally, and
smb347 reports USB online without a cable, so power-off always restarted.

---
--- a/drivers/soc/tegra/pmc.c	2026-11-23 20:52:09.292770728 +0000
+++ b/drivers/soc/tegra/pmc.c	2026-11-23 20:52:09.296950102 +0000
@@ -1291,20 +1291,14 @@
 
 static int tegra_pmc_power_off_handler(struct sys_off_data *data)
 {
-	struct tegra_pmc *pmc = data->cb_data;
-
 	/*
-	 * Reboot Nexus 7 into special bootloader mode if USB cable is
-	 * connected in order to display battery status and power off.
+	 * Second Chapter: upstream reboots the Nexus 7 into a special mode of
+	 * Google's original bootloader here when a USB cable is connected, to
+	 * show the battery status. U-Boot has no such mode and simply starts
+	 * the system again. And smb347 reports USB as online even with no
+	 * cable, so every power-off became a restart. Do nothing, so the
+	 * MAX77663 power chip switches the tablet off.
 	 */
-	if (of_machine_is_compatible("asus,grouper") &&
-	    power_supply_is_system_supplied()) {
-		const u32 go_to_charger_mode = 0xa5a55a5a;
-
-		tegra_pmc_writel(pmc, go_to_charger_mode, PMC_SCRATCH37);
-		tegra_pmc_restart(pmc);
-	}
-
 	return NOTIFY_DONE;
 }
 
